- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/compare.html
- Summary (EN): The Compare node creates a 0 to 1 mask by testing two layers, VDBs or attributes against each other pixel by pixel. If input B is not wired, the first input is compared with a constant Comparison Value.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Compare produit un masque de 0 à 1 en comparant pixel par pixel deux entrées selon une condition choisie, avec une tolérance et une chute réglables.

- Inputs meaning: ["A: layer, VDB or attribute to compare", "B: layer, VDB or attribute to compare with (any type convertible to A's type)", "tolerance (optional): mono per-pixel tolerance"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by source", "Comparison Value: constant compared against each channel of A when B is not wired", "Tolerance: band around the comparison that gets soft mask values (both sides for equality, one side for strict inequality)", "True If: condition that sets the mask to 1 (==, !=, >, >=, <, <=)", "Components: True if All or True if Any channel passes", "Falloff: None (hard cutoff), Linear, or Elendt (smooth S-curve)"]

- Caveats: ["For multi-channel inputs the Components setting decides the result", "Comparison Value is ignored when B is wired", "The page's description of the mask output is somewhat ambiguous next to True If", "Not the same node as Compare and Blend (compareblend)"]

